# Swift core (`NagaCore` + `NagaUSB`)

## Modules

- `NagaCore` (lib): `Protocol/` (pure encoders, CRC), `USB/Transport.swift` (`Transport` + `IOKitTransport`),
  `Driver.swift` (apply sequences), `Models.swift`, `Store.swift`, `API.swift`. No UI types here.
- `NagaUSB` (C): thin IOKit bridge (`naga_usb_open` / `naga_usb_set_report` / `naga_usb_list`). No protocol logic.
- `NagaCLI` (bin): `naga-cli info|apply [--profile ID]|rgb <effect> [#hex]|dpi <x>|poll <hz>|off`.
- `NagaCoreSmoke` (bin): golden-byte / migration / sequence checks (Command Line Tools have no XCTest).

Ask before adding third-party SPM dependencies.

## Public API (mirror upstream IPC one-to-one, all synchronous)

```swift
scanDevice() -> FfiDeviceInfo
readStore() -> FfiProfileStore
writeStore(store:) -> FfiProfileStore
upsertProfile(profile:) / deleteProfile(id:) / duplicateProfile(id:) / setActiveProfile(id:) -> FfiProfileStore
applyProfile(profile:) -> FfiApplyResult
previewRgb(rgb:) -> FfiApplyResult
setRgbOff() -> FfiApplyResult
getSettings() -> FfiAppSettings / updateSettings(partial:) -> FfiAppSettings
setStoreDir(path:)
createEmptyProfile(name:) -> FfiNagaProfile
```

Type names keep the `Ffi*` prefix for drop-in parity with the previous UniFFI surface used by the SwiftUI app.

- UI calls these via `CoreClient` on a background executor. Core functions block (USB sleeps use `Thread.sleep`).
- Guard the cached interface and the store file with locks; calls may arrive from multiple threads.
- No async/await inside `NagaCore`. Upstream's async is only the Node event loop.

## Errors

- Driver ops never throw to the app. They return `FfiApplyResult { ok, message, key, params, stage }` exactly like upstream:
  `driverNotices.applyComplete`, `.applyCompleteWithMacros` (`macroCount`), `.rgbUpdated`, `.rgbOff`,
  `.notFound`, `.usbError` (`detail`). `message` is the German fallback text from upstream.
- Device missing → `key = driverNotices.notFound`.
- Store read failure (missing or corrupt JSON) → return a fresh initial store. Never crash.

## Style

- Protocol constants live next to their encoder (`txDefault`, `ledClass`, …).
- Encoders take validated domain values, clamp like upstream, and return a 90-byte `Report`.
- Keep MIT attribution; no Razer Synapse code.

## Tests

- Golden-byte checks for every encoder and CRC via `swift run naga-core-smoke`.
- Recorded-transport checks for apply sequences (`razer-protocol.mdc`).
- Store migration checks: legacy array, pre-wheel-tilt, v2.
- Hardware tests are manual via `naga-cli`.
